WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.379
What happens when you place a ship in a bottle
into the Clockworks?

00:00:03.379 --> 00:00:08.590
Dr. Westrin prepared three ships, each in
their own glass bottle, for experimentation.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:12.760
The first ship was placed on the setting "Coarse,"
and it produced a pile of glass shards, a

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.000
pile of woodshavings, and a pile of cloth
scraps.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.320
The next ship was placed on the setting "1:1,"
and the output produced was a wooden bottle,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.349
containing a glass model ship.

00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:26.259
The final bottle was placed on the setting
"Very Fine," and it produced a glass bottle

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:30.789
containing a small model of the International
Space Station, apparently constructed from

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:33.199
the very same wood as the original ship.

